# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Habit Tracker — Frontend environment variables (Vite)
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in the values. `.env` is gitignored.
# Every var must be prefixed with VITE_ to be exposed to the browser.
# Tags: [REQUIRED] = app won't work without it · [OPTIONAL] = enables a feature
#
# ⚠️ THESE ARE BAKED IN AT BUILD TIME. Vite substitutes import.meta.env.* into the
#    bundle when you build — it is NOT a runtime lookup. So on Vercel, adding or
#    changing any var here does nothing until you REDEPLOY. Nothing in this file is
#    secret: everything below ships to the browser and is readable by anyone.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# [REQUIRED FOR PRODUCTION BUILDS] Backend API base URL, no trailing slash.
#   The production build FAILS if this is unset (vite.config.js) — otherwise the
#   deployed bundle would permanently point at localhost.
#   Local dev:   leave empty. client.js falls back to a relative '/api' and the
#                Vite dev proxy forwards it to http://localhost:3000.
#   Production:  https://<your-app>.onrender.com/api
VITE_API_URL=

# [OPTIONAL] Web Push public key — shows the reminders UI when set.
#   Must equal VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY in the backend .env.
VITE_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=

# [OPTIONAL] Google Sign-In client ID — the button only renders when this is set,
#   so an unset value in a Vercel build = no Google button on the deployed site.
#   Must equal GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID in the backend .env, AND your deployed origin must
#   be listed under "Authorized JavaScript origins" in Google Cloud Console →
#   Credentials → your OAuth client (e.g. https://your-app.vercel.app, no path).
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
